\begin_layout Subsection
Broadcast Encryption [Fiat–Naor 94]
\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition

\begin_inset Argument 1
status collapsed


\begin_layout Standard
Broadcast encryption
\end_layout

\end_inset

A broadcast-encryption scheme for 
\begin_inset Formula $N$
\end_inset

 recipients consists of a setup algorithm producing keys 
\begin_inset Formula $(K_1,\ldots,K_N)$
\end_inset

, an encryption map 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
\operatorname{Enc}:
\mathcal{M}\times2^{[N]}\times\mathcal{K}^N\longrightarrow\mathcal{C},
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

and decryption maps 
\begin_inset Formula $\operatorname{Dec}_i$
\end_inset

. Correctness requires that for every 
\begin_inset Formula $M\in\mathcal{M}$
\end_inset

, every 
\begin_inset Formula $S\subseteq[N]$
\end_inset

, and every 
\begin_inset Formula $i\in S$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
\operatorname{Dec}_i(K_i,
\operatorname{Enc}(M,S,K_1,\ldots,K_N))=M.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

Privacy requires that every coalition contained in 
\begin_inset Formula $[N]\setminus S$
\end_inset

 obtain no information about 
\begin_inset Formula $M$
\end_inset

 from the ciphertext and its keys. 
\end_layout

