 Secret Sharing: Syntax
\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition

\begin_inset Argument 1
status collapsed


\begin_layout Standard
Threshold secret sharing
\end_layout

\end_inset


\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "def:threshold-secret-sharing"

\end_inset

 Let 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{S}$
\end_inset

 be a finite secret space, let 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{R}$
\end_inset

 be a finite randomness space, and let 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{S}_1,\ldots,\mathcal{S}_n$
\end_inset

 be share spaces. A 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset

-out-of-
\begin_inset Formula $n$
\end_inset

 secret-sharing scheme consists of a randomized dealing map 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{align*}
\mathcal{E}:\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{R}
&\longrightarrow
\mathcal{S}_1\times\cdots\times\mathcal{S}_n
\end{align*}
\end_inset

and, for every 
\begin_inset Formula $T\subseteq[n]$
\end_inset

 with 
\begin_inset Formula $|T|=t$
\end_inset

, a deterministic reconstruction map 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
\mathcal{D}_T:\prod_{i\in T}\mathcal{S}_i\longrightarrow\mathcal{S}.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Dealing Function
\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition

\begin_inset Argument 1
status collapsed


\begin_layout Standard
Share notation
\end_layout

\end_inset

For 
\begin_inset Formula $(s_1,\ldots,s_n)=\mathcal{E}(s;r)$
\end_inset

, write 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
s_T=(s_i)_{i\in T}.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\begin_inset Separator plain

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Definition

\begin_inset Argument 1
status collapsed


\begin_layout Standard
Perfect privacy
\end_layout

\end_inset

The distribution of any 
\begin_inset Formula $t-1$
\end_inset

 shares 
\begin_inset Formula $s_{i_1},\ldots,s_{i_{t-1}}$
\end_inset

 is independent of the secret 
\begin_inset Formula $s$
\end_inset

. Formally, for every pair 
\begin_inset Formula $s,s'\in\mathcal{S}$
\end_inset

 and every coalition 
\begin_inset Formula $T\subseteq[n]$
\end_inset

 with 
\begin_inset Formula $|T|<t$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
\bigl(\mathcal{E}_i(s;r)\bigr)_{i\in T}
\equiv
\bigl(\mathcal{E}_i(s';r)\bigr)_{i\in T}.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset


\end_layout

