\begin_inset Formula $r_i=a_i$
\end_inset

. The equality 
\begin_inset Formula $s_n=a_n$
\end_inset

 then uniquely fixes 
\begin_inset Formula $r_j$
\end_inset

, since the map 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
r_j\longmapsto
-\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}r_i\right)+s
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

is a bijection of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{S}$
\end_inset

