\begin_layout Subsubsection
Linear Secret-Sharing Formulation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $f_x:\mathbb{F}^m\to\mathbb{F}$
\end_inset

 be linear and suppose that designated vectors 
\begin_inset Formula $v_1,\ldots,v_N\in\mathbb{F}^m$
\end_inset

 satisfy 
\begin_inset Formula $f_x(v_i)=x[i]$
\end_inset

. If 
\begin_inset Formula $v_i=q_1+q_2$
\end_inset

 is additively shared so that each 
\begin_inset Formula $q_s$
\end_inset

 is uniform, then linearity gives 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
f_x(q_1)+f_x(q_2)=f_x(v_i)=x[i].
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

Consequently, additive secret sharing of the designated vector yields a two-server PIR whenever the shares have index-independent marginals.
\end_layout

