\begin_layout Proof
Replace 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{F}_2$
\end_inset

 in the preceding multilinear construction by a field 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{F}$
\end_inset

 of characteristic greater than three, and sample 
\begin_inset Formula $r,s,t\xleftarrow{R}\mathbb{F}^m$
\end_inset

. Use the two queries 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
q_0=(r,s,t),
\qquad q_1=(r+e_i,s+e_j,t+e_k).
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

Define 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
P(\lambda)=f_x(r+\lambda e_i,s+\lambda e_j,t+\lambda e_k).
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

This polynomial has degree at most three, and its coefficient of 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda^3$
\end_inset

 is 
\begin_inset Formula $f_x(e_i,e_j,e_k)=x[i,j,k]$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Proof
Server 
\begin_inset Formula $b\in\{0,1\}$
\end_inset

 returns 
\begin_inset Formula $P(b)$
\end_inset

 and all 
\begin_inset Formula $3m$
\end_inset

 first partial derivatives of 
\begin_inset Formula $f_x$
\end_inset

 at 
\begin_inset Formula $q_b$
\end_inset

. By the chain rule, these values determine 
\begin_inset Formula $P'(b)$
\end_inset

. The Hermite data 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
P(0),P'(0),P(1),P'(1)
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

uniquely determine 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

, because the field has characteristic different from 
\begin_inset Formula $2$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $3$
\end_inset

. The coefficient of 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda^3$
\end_inset

 is 
\begin_inset Formula $x[i,j,k]$
\end_inset

. Both queries are uniform, and each answer contains 
\begin_inset Formula $3m+1$
\end_inset

 field elements. 
\end_layout

