\begin_layout Proof
For a requested index 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

, sample 
\begin_inset Formula $r\xleftarrow{R}\mathbb{F}^m$
\end_inset

 and define 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
q_\ell=v_i+\ell r,
\qquad
a_\ell=f_x(q_\ell),
\qquad \ell\in\{1,2,3\}.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

The univariate polynomial 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
P(T)=f_x(v_i+Tr)
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

has degree at most two. The decoder interpolates 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

 from 
\begin_inset Formula $P(1),P(2),P(3)$
\end_inset

 and outputs 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
P(0)=f_x(v_i)=x[i].
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

For every nonzero 
\begin_inset Formula $\ell$
\end_inset

, multiplication by 
\begin_inset Formula $\ell$
\end_inset

 is a permutation of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{F}^m$
\end_inset

; hence 
\begin_inset Formula $q_\ell$
\end_inset

 is uniform and independent of 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

. 
\end_layout

