\begin_layout Definition

\begin_inset Argument 1
status collapsed


\begin_layout Standard
Fully homomorphic encryption
\end_layout

\end_inset

An FHE scheme consists of the following four probabilistic algorithms, each running in polynomial time: 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{align*}
(pk,sk)&\leftarrow\operatorname{KeyGen}(1^\lambda),\\
c&\leftarrow\operatorname{Enc}_{pk}(m),\\
c'&\leftarrow\operatorname{Eval}_{pk}(C,c_1,\ldots,c_t),\\
m'&=\operatorname{Dec}_{sk}(c').
\end{align*}
\end_inset

Correctness requires that for every circuit 
\begin_inset Formula $C$
\end_inset

 and messages 
\begin_inset Formula $m_1,\ldots,m_t$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{multline*}
\operatorname{Dec}_{sk}\bigl(
\operatorname{Eval}_{pk}(C,
\operatorname{Enc}_{pk}(m_1),\ldots,
\operatorname{Enc}_{pk}(m_t))\bigr)\\
=C(m_1,\ldots,m_t)
\end{multline*}
\end_inset

except with negligible probability. Compactness requires the evaluated ciphertext length to be bounded by a polynomial in 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda$
\end_inset

 and the output length of 
\begin_inset Formula $C$
\end_inset

, independently of 
\begin_inset Formula $|C|$
\end_inset

. Security is semantic security of the underlying encryption scheme. 
\end_layout

