\begin_inset Formula $s^1_i$
\end_inset

 independently. Sample 
\begin_inset Formula $b^0\xleftarrow{R}\mathbb{F}_2^L$
\end_inset

 and set 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
b^1=b^0+e_i.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

Define 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
\Delta=e_j+G(s^0_i)+G(s^1_i)\in\mathbb{F}_2^M
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

and give server 
\begin_inset Formula $p$
\end_inset

 the key 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
K_p=(s^p_1,\ldots,s^p_L,b^p,\Delta).
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

The 
\begin_inset Formula $\ell$
\end_inset

-th block of 
\begin_inset Formula $\operatorname{Expand}(K_p)$
\end_inset

 is 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
Q_{p,\ell}=G(s^p_\ell)+b^p_\ell\Delta.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset


