 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\beta\in G$
\end_inset

, define the point function 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
f_{\alpha,\beta}:\{0,1\}^n\longrightarrow G
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

by 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
f_{\alpha,\beta}(\alpha)=\beta,
\qquad
f_{\alpha,\beta}(x)=0\quad\text{for }x\neq\alpha.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

A distributed point function is an FSS scheme for the family 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
\{f_{\alpha,\beta}:\alpha\in\{0,1\}^n,\ \beta\in G\}.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset


