\begin_layout Subsubsection
Construction from a Linear PIR Identity
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Let 
\begin_inset Formula $G$
\end_inset

 be a finite abelian group. Assume that for every database 
\begin_inset Formula $D$
\end_inset

 there is a homomorphism 
\begin_inset Formula $H_D:G^m\to G$
\end_inset

 and that every index 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

 has an associated 
\begin_inset Formula $u_x\in G^m$
\end_inset

 satisfying, for every 
\begin_inset Formula $r\in G^m$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
H_D(r)-H_D(r+u_x)=D[x].
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

For a scalar secret 
\begin_inset Formula $s$
\end_inset

, replace 
\begin_inset Formula $u_x$
\end_inset

 by 
\begin_inset Formula $s u_x$
\end_inset

. By linearity, 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
H_D(r)-H_D(r+s\cdot u_x)=D[x]\cdot s.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

The decoder therefore obtains 
\begin_inset Formula $D[x]s$
\end_inset

. This identity gives a CDS whenever the two induced query marginals are independent of 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

 and, on inputs with 
\begin_inset Formula $D[x]=0$
\end_inset

, their joint distribution is independent of 
\begin_inset Formula $s$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

