\begin_layout Definition

\begin_inset Argument 1
status collapsed


\begin_layout Standard
Amortized CDS complexity
\end_layout

\end_inset

Let 
\begin_inset Formula $\operatorname{CDS}(f,L)$
\end_inset

 denote the CDS communication for an 
\begin_inset Formula $L$
\end_inset

-bit secret per party. Correctness requires communicating at least the 
\begin_inset Formula $L$
\end_inset

 bits that are released on accepting inputs, while independent repetition of a one-bit protocol gives the upper bound 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
L\leq\operatorname{CDS}(f,L)
\leq L\cdot\operatorname{CDS}(f,1).
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

Define the asymptotic overhead by 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
\overline{\operatorname{CDS}}(f)
=\liminf_{L\to\infty}
\frac{\operatorname{CDS}(f,L)}{L}.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Theorem

\begin_inset Argument 1
status collapsed


\begin_layout Standard
