\end_layout

\end_inset

Fix predicates 
\begin_inset Formula $f_1,ldots,f_T:X\times Y\to\{0,1\}$
\end_inset

 and a secret space 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{S}$
\end_inset

. A batch CDS consists of two message algorithms and a decoder. For every input pair 
\begin_inset Formula $(x,y)$
\end_inset

 and secret vector 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{s}=(s_1,ldots,s_T)$
\end_inset

, correctness requires recovery of 
\begin_inset Formula $(s_i)_{i:f_i(x,y)=1}$
\end_inset

. Privacy requires that, for every two secret vectors 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{s},\boldsymbol{s}'$
\end_inset

 agreeing on all accepting coordinates, the two joint transcript distributions are identical. 
\end_layout

