\begin_layout Subsubsection
Multiplication and Degree Reduction
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Suppose 
\begin_inset Formula $a_i=p(i)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $b_i=q(i)$
\end_inset

 are degree-
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset

 shares of 
\begin_inset Formula $a$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $b$
\end_inset

. Each party locally computes 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
c_i=a_i b_i.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

These are evaluations of the degree-
\begin_inset Formula $2t$
\end_inset

 polynomial 
\begin_inset Formula $p(X)q(X)$
\end_inset

. Since 
\begin_inset Formula $n>2t$
\end_inset

, there are public interpolation coefficients 
\begin_inset Formula $\alpha_1,\ldots,\alpha_n$
