\begin_inset Formula $(P,V)$
\end_inset

 for 
\begin_inset Formula $L$
\end_inset

 is zero knowledge if, for every cheating verifier 
\begin_inset Formula $V^*$
\end_inset

, there exists a simulator 
\begin_inset Formula $S$
\end_inset

, with the same complexity as 
\begin_inset Formula $V^*$
\end_inset

, such that for every 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in L$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
\langle P(x)\leftrightarrow V^*(x)\rangle_V
\equiv
S(V^*,x).
\end{equation*}
\end_inset


\end_layout

