\begin_inset Formula $\pi$
\end_inset

, and the verifier queries only a few random locations of 
\begin_inset Formula $\pi$
\end_inset

. A strong version of the BFL theorem is known as the PCP theorem, with applications to hardness of approximation, cryptography, and more.
