\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "def:pcp"

\end_inset

 Let 
\begin_inset Formula $L\subseteq\{0,1\}^*$
\end_inset

. A PCP system consists of a prover 
\begin_inset Formula $P$
\end_inset

 that produces an oracle string 
\begin_inset Formula $\Pi$
\end_inset

 and a probabilistic oracle verifier 
\begin_inset Formula $V$
\end_inset

. For functions 
\begin_inset Formula $r,q:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{N}$
\end_inset

 and soundness error 
\begin_inset Formula $\varepsilon$
\end_inset

, the verifier uses at most 
\begin_inset Formula $r(|x|)$
\end_inset

 random bits, makes at most 
\begin_inset Formula $q(|x|)$
\end_inset

 oracle queries, and satisfies: 
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate

\emph on
Completeness:
\emph default
 for every 
\begin_inset Formula $x\in L$
\end_inset

, there exists 
\begin_inset Formula $\Pi$
\end_inset

 such that 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
\Pr[V^\Pi(x)=1]=1.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\emph on
Soundness:
\emph default
 for every 
\begin_inset Formula $x\notin L$
\end_inset

 and every oracle string 
\begin_inset Formula $\Pi^*$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
\Pr[V^{\Pi^*}(x)=1]\leq\varepsilon.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Subsection
From Interactive Proofs to PCPs
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The construction converts an interactive proof satisfying Definition
\begin_inset space ~

\end_inset


