\begin_layout Definition

\begin_inset Argument 1
status collapsed


\begin_layout Standard
Zero sub-cube proof
\end_layout

\end_inset

The proof has completeness 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
Q|_{H^\ell}\equiv0
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\Pr_{\Pi\leftarrow P(Q)}[V(Q,\Pi)=1]=1,
\end{equation*}
\end_inset

and soundness 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation*}
Q|_{H^\ell}\not\equiv0
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\forall\Pi^*:\Pr[V(Q,\Pi^*)=1]\leq\frac12.
\end{equation*}
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The idea is that 
\begin_inset Formula $Q|_{H^\ell}\equiv0$
\end_inset

 if and only if 
\begin_inset Formula $\widetilde Q\equiv0$
\end_inset

, where 
\begin_inset Formula $\widetilde Q$
\end_inset

 is the LDE of 
\begin_inset Formula $Q$
\end_inset

. The problem is checking that 
\begin_inset Formula $\widetilde Q$
\end_inset

 is really the LDE of 
\begin_inset Formula $Q$
\end_inset

. The variables are linearized one by one, as in the 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathsf{IP}=\mathsf{PSPACE}$
\end_inset

 protocol.
\end_layout

